    <section id="why-radio">
      <h2>Why Far Reach Radio Fits Live Play</h2>
      <p>
        Far Reach Radio is built for session music and ambience, not for managing bot permissions or spending game
        time inside a heavy audio control surface.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>One host panel</strong> - control the session soundtrack from one browser tab.</li>
        <li><strong>One listener link</strong> - players open the same link and hear the same stream timeline.</li>
        <li><strong>No player accounts</strong> - only the host needs to log in.</li>
        <li><strong>Scene-ready playlists</strong> - jump between combat, tavern, travel, horror, mystery, and victory moods without rebuilding audio from scratch.</li>
        <li><strong>Works online or in person</strong> - share the link remotely or run it through a speaker at the table.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="host-flow">
      <h2>How Hosts Run Music Fast</h2>
      <p>Far Reach Radio is designed for fast setup before session start and quick control while scenes are moving.</p>
      <figure class="toolshot-card toolshot-card--smallshot">
        <img
          src="/assets/screen_shots/radio_host_control.png"
          alt="Far Reach Radio host control panel with shareable listener link and playlist controls."
          loading="lazy"
        />
        <figcaption>Host control panel for sharing the listener URL, starting playlists, and tracking what is currently playing.</figcaption>
      </figure>

      <h3>1. Start A Channel</h3>
      <p>
        Head to <a href="https://radio.farreachco.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener">radio.farreachco.com</a> and enter a channel name.
        That opens your host control panel.
      </p>

      <h3>2. Choose Session Music</h3>
      <p>
        Pick a playlist for the current scene. Music starts immediately, and you can switch playlists as the tone changes.
      </p>

      <h3>3. Share The Listener Link</h3>
      <p>
        Copy the listener URL and send it to players in Discord, text, or email. They click, press play, and join the live session audio.
      </p>

      <h3>4. Run Music During Play</h3>
      <p>
        As host, you can switch playlists, skip tracks, or stop the stream. The panel always shows what is currently playing.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="playlist-library">
      <h2>RPG Music Playlist Library With 200+ Original Pieces</h2>
      <p>
        The library is organized around scene types, so you can move with the session instead of digging through generic playlists.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Combat and battle</strong> - stronger energy for fights and major encounters.</li>
        <li><strong>Exploration and travel</strong> - movement-friendly music for wilderness, dungeon, and road scenes.</li>
        <li><strong>Tavern and town</strong> - lighter social music for downtime and roleplay.</li>
        <li><strong>Horror and suspense</strong> - darker ambience for tension, dread, and weird scenes.</li>
        <li><strong>Mystery and intrigue</strong> - subtler sound for investigation and social pressure.</li>
        <li><strong>Triumph and celebration</strong> - stronger payoff music for victories and milestones.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Free accounts get the standard library. Pro unlocks the full catalog with additional exclusive playlists and deeper coverage across moods and scenarios.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="discord-alternative">
      <h2>Alternative To Discord Music Bots For D&amp;D Sessions</h2>
      <p>
        The strongest search signal we have so far is around Discord bot alternatives, and that makes sense: this tool removes the bot-management layer from the workflow.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Less setup friction</strong> - no bot installs, slash commands, or permission troubleshooting.</li>
        <li><strong>Cleaner session control</strong> - use one host surface built for moving between RPG scenes quickly.</li>
        <li><strong>Predictable listening</strong> - everyone hears the same server stream instead of manually lining up tracks.</li>
        <li><strong>Link-based access</strong> - players join by URL instead of navigating bot-specific commands.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        If that is the comparison you are making, read <a href="/discord-music-bot-alternative">Discord Music Bot Alternative</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="syrinscape-comparison">
      <h2>Where Far Reach Radio Sits Against Syrinscape</h2>
      <p>
        If you are comparing this against Syrinscape, the main difference is workflow. Far Reach Radio is lighter and more playlist-driven during live play.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Far Reach Radio fits better when</strong> you want one host panel, one listener link, original scene playlists, and less table-time spent operating audio software.</li>
        <li><strong>Far Reach Radio fits better when</strong> you want a straightforward session soundtrack layer that supports play without becoming its own mini-game.</li>
        <li><strong>Syrinscape may still fit better when</strong> you want a deeper sound-set ecosystem, more elaborate audio construction, or a bigger long-established sound library.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        For the direct comparison page, see <a href="/syrinscape-alternative">Syrinscape Alternative</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="online-and-in-person">
      <h2>Use It For Online Groups Or In-Person Tables</h2>
      <p>
        Far Reach Radio works well for remote sessions, hybrid games, and in-person tables that still want centralized music control.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Online groups</strong> - send the listener link to everyone and keep the soundtrack in sync.</li>
        <li><strong>In-person games</strong> - open the listener link on a speaker-connected device and control playlists from your laptop or phone.</li>
        <li><strong>Recurring campaigns</strong> - reuse channel names for the same group and keep your music flow consistent from session to session.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Hosting requires a free <a href="https://farreachco.com/register">Far Reach Co. account</a>. Listeners do not need accounts.
      </p>
