    <section id="faq">
      <h2>Common Questions About Tabletop RPG Music Online</h2>

      <h3>How do I play D&amp;D music online with my players?</h3>
      <p>Create a channel, choose a playlist, and share the listener link. Players open the link and hear the same stream in sync.</p>

      <h3>Do my players need an account?</h3>
      <p>No. Only the host needs an account. Listeners can tune in with just the link.</p>

      <h3>Is this an alternative to Discord music bots?</h3>
      <p>Yes. It replaces bot commands and voice-channel routing with one host panel and one listener link.</p>

      <h3>Is this an alternative to Syrinscape?</h3>
      <p>It can be, especially if you want a lighter playlist-driven workflow. If you want a bigger sound-set ecosystem and deeper audio construction, Syrinscape may still be the better fit.</p>

      <h3>Can I use this for in-person games?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Open the listener link on a speaker-connected device and use the host panel on your phone or laptop.</p>

      <h3>Does the music keep playing if I close the host panel?</h3>
      <p>Yes. Once a playlist is started, the server continues streaming while listeners are connected. The stream goes idle after 10 minutes with no listeners.</p>

      <h3>Can multiple people host on the same channel?</h3>
      <p>Any logged-in user can send commands to a channel. If another GM needs to take over music duties, they can open the host panel for the same channel name.</p>
    </section>

